                                                            25
                                 CHAPTER 4

                THE COURSE OF LIFE
       PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

The Course of Life

When a person gets the course of life and the times of life right, such
person is headed for greatness, fulfillment and success. The course of
life talks about the sequential unraveling of events and the progression
of happenings in one’s life. The course of life- the events along the paths
of a life, determines where a life is headed. It is important to pay great
attention to the course of one’s lives and make sure it is trending in the
positive direction.

One of the areas of confusion in people ordering the course of their lives
is in understanding the balance between God’s predestination and
human choices. There are people who believe that the events, courses
and timings of life are predestined by God and merely unfold as we live
on earth. Thus, there are people who believe that there is virtually
nothing a person can do outside of God’s solid-cast predestination for
them. These ‘fatalists’ believe that God is the author and designer of
every man’s destiny and each person merely lives out God’s script for
them. Thus, ‘the rich is rich because God willed it and the poor is poor
because God willed it’, so they believe.

                                                              26
                                      TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

On the other opposite end of the spectrum are those who believe that
man is the architect of his destiny and ultimate pilot of the course of
his life. These categories of people believe that predestination is a
farce and man rules his life by his choices. The extremists in this
school of thought have even suggested that God is a myth and man is
the grand commander of his own destiny. Some milder point of view
in this humanistic philosophy believe that God exists but does not
determine the destiny of anyone - each person’s life is ultimately what
he or she makes of it. Man, they say, is the master of his fate.
Therefore, it is important to get answers and discover the truth and
balance in the above points of view. Does God have a predestined
and preordained outcome for each person’s lives? Is the outcome of
everyone’s life absolutely based on their choice or God’s
preordination? Are these two mutually exclusive - meaning, is it either
one or the other? Are they mutually inclusive – meaning, can both
concepts work together?
The answers to the above questions will be discovered in this chapter
and the truths will be revolutionary for those that apply them.

The Mystery of Predestination

Ps. 139:13-18 expresses vital thoughts on the concept on predestination:
You made all the delicate, inner parts of my body and knit me together in
my mother's womb. Thank you for making me so wonderfully complex!
Your workmanship is marvelous—how well I know it. You watched me as
I was being formed in utter seclusion, as I was woven together in the dark
of the womb. You saw me before I was born. Every day of my life was
recorded in your book. Every moment was laid out before a single day had
passed. How precious are your thoughts about me, O God. They cannot
be numbered! I can't even count them; they outnumber the grains of sand!
And when I wake up, you are still with me! (NLT).

                                                            27
                  THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

What a statement, ‘You saw me before I was born. Every day of my life
was recorded in your book. Every moment was laid out before a single
day had passed’! This scripture shows that God has actually written
out things about every person even before they come to the earth. It
proves that people are deployed by God to the earth to live out what
is written concerning them. As written in Heb.10:7-9, Christ said,
‘Look, I have come to do your will, O God—as is written about me in
the Scriptures.' Therefore, Jesus our perfect example had His destiny
written and set before He came to the earth.
Any one that understands scriptures know that preordination and
predestination are truths in God. In Jer.1: 5, we see that before
Jeremiah was born, God had predetermined what He wanted to
become of him. Jer.1:5 says, "I knew you before I formed you in your
mother's womb. Before you were born I set you apart and appointed you
as my prophet to the nations’’. This announcement came before
Jeremiah started the ministry God committed into his hand. God
obviously predestines and preordains, it is everyone’s duty to discover
their preordination and walk in it.

Rom. 8:29-30 says, for whom He foreknew, He also predestined to be
conformed to the image of His Son, that He might be the firstborn
among many brethren. Moreover whom He predestined, these He also
called; whom He called, these He also justified; and whom He justified,
these He also glorified. God truly has what He has written in His
books concerning everyone. Rev. 20:12 records, and I saw the dead,
small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and
another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were
judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to
their works (NKJV). The Book of Life is where the name of everyone
who receives eternal salvation through Jesus Christ is written.

                                                            28
                                      TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

The other books are books of records where the preordinations and
the actual deeds of everyone who came to the earth are written. On
the day of judgment, everyone’s deeds will be measured against their
preordinations; if all one’s deeds are out of alignment the preordained
assignment, then the entire work-done is judged zero. Many religions
have emphasized imminent judgment based on the record of the good
deeds versus bad deeds of men but do not make people conscious of
coming judgment based on the record of the believer’s preordination
versus their actual course lived. The book of preordination and
record determine rewards while the Book of Life, on its own part,
decides eternal abode - heaven or hell. A lot of believers are taught
that rewards in heaven are based on good deeds on earth. They miss
the vital truth that reward in heaven is assignment-based. You must
know that God does not reward you just because you do the good
things but because you do the right things. The right things are the
things that He has preordained for you to do. Thus, the ultimate
questions on the last day are two - Did you accept Jesus Christ as
savior and Lord while on earth? Did you do the things that you were
sent to the earth to do? Every other question is an addendum.

Predestination Versus Choice?

When a truth is misapplied or misappropriated, it produces the same
effect as a lie. It is true that the course of every person’s life has been
preordained but it is not true the events of people’s lives have been
cast-in-stone by God, such that things are bound to happen in a
person’s life by God’s preordination with or without the person’s
participation.

                                                            29
                  THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

God is a God of purpose and His purpose for a matter is described by
the resultant end of the matter. Thus, for everything God does, He
has an intended end in mind. In other words, there is something God
is trying to achieve in everything He does. Therefore, God said, ‘I
declare the end from the beginning, and from ancient times things
that are not yet done, Saying, 'My counsel shall stand, And I will do
all My pleasure’ (Isa. 46:10). This statement means that what God is
trying to do and, the end He has in mind is preordained and must
surely happen. Thus, God preordains the resultant end but He is
flexible in the means to achieve the end.

Generally, in life, the end is superior to the means. In fact, the end
determines if the means is worthwhile or not. The end talks about
what one is trying to achieve, the means describes how one goes
about achieving it. If the means outweighs the end, purpose has been
defeated. Therefore, means may change even when the end is fixed.

God declares the end from the beginning! Thus, God is very
interested in the end and therefore, God predestined the end. In other
words, what God is trying to achieve in every situation is cast in stone
and has been predestined to be surely achieved because God cannot
fail. However, God changes the means to achieve His end due to the
choices of the human factors involved.
The reason for confusion among many people on the issue of
preordination and choices is in not realizing that every human being,
the entirety of the human race and all the events of the lifetimes of the
entire people who have lived on the earth, with all the courses of all
their lives on earth - are all part of the means to an end. The end,
which is God’s ultimate purpose, is higher than each of us and every
one of us.

                                                            30
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

This is why, despite the truth of predestination, nothing is irrevocably
fixed for anyone as a predestined personal life outcome. Volume one of
this book series makes us to understand that the end of all things in
God’s mind is ‘His Kingdom Come’ eternally on the earth. The series of
events that are fixed for the Kingdom Story to be fulfilled MUST
happen by predestination. The human agents that will fulfill the
predestination will do so based on their choices.

For example, God predestined that Divinity would come to the earth,
born by a virgin without sin, and would deliver humanity from sin and
Satan. That was an end to be achieved; every other thing that happened
from the fall of man to the coming of Jesus was a means to that end.
Every man and woman that played a role from Adam to Abraham to
David to the ascension of Jesus Christ in the story of Redemption did
so based on their choices. If they did not, God would have passed
through someone else to get the preordination of salvation fulfilled
because the story was predestined to be fulfilled.

Right now, there is the predestination that the kingdoms of the earth
and all the spheres and sectors of the world system will bow to the
Lordship of Jesus, the people that will fulfill this preordination in each
different sphere of the world will partner with it by their choices. Also,
we are currently on earth to practice dominion and qualify for the level
of kingdom rule we can be trusted with when the Kingdom of God
comes physically upon the earth. We qualify for levels of influence in
the Soon Coming Kingdom by our present level demonstration of
Kingdom interest and dominion in today’s world as the Kingdom is
being won.

                                                              31
                    THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

Jesus is coming back to restate the Kingdom on the earth and rule and
reign with His saints. Satan and His cohorts will be judged and thrown
into eternal damnation. A new earth and a new heaven will be made
and we will rule over the systems of the earths as co-regents with Jesus
Christ. All these are predestined event but the roles, timings and
alignment of individuals and systems is based on their choices.

Infinite Routes to Fulfill Predestined End

God has infinite ways and possibilities in His Infinite-Mind on how
each end result can be achieved. Thus, He preordains events and people
into roles in order to achieve His predestined end. However, if anyone is
not aligned by their choices along the path of predestination, they have
not hurt the plan; they have only denied themselves the privilege of
being part of the plan. There are infinite options of people and events
that God can pass through as means to His predestined end. Because
He is God - all the means are programmed into His predestination from
the onset so there is a predestined role for everyone but not cast-in-
stone for them.

The reason people get confused about predestination is because they
think their lives is ‘an end’. So, they view predestination from the
myopic perspective of ‘predestination for their lives’. No! Your life is a
‘means to an end’. The predestination is not about you, it is about
something you are to do which is merely a work function in the eternal
predestined project of God. Thus, if you do not do it, it will still be done
nonetheless. It is important to note that your life, marriage, business,
career, ministry, academics and so on, are all means. God’s kingdom
coming is the end. People regard their lives as an end because they are
judging life based on their micro-view of self.

                                                              32
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

God has things He is trying to achieve in your world, territory, city,
family that He has predestined to happen. You are part of the
predestined means to that predestined end. But remember that means
are changeable, plans are revisable and people are disposable. Thus,
predestination is real but every person is only an available alternative as
a means in achieving God’s predestined end. So, you have a predestined
role to play in God’s scheme of predestined purpose. The role must be
played and the end result must happen. However, whether it is you that
will play the role and how far you will go in playing the role depends on
your choices.

The Powers inherent in Man

God has ordained the events, timings and course of life for every person
before they were born but it is completely their choices to be aligned or
unaligned with it. God has given much power to man and He will never
violate it even to get His utmost will done. Thus, God has a
predestination for everyone but it is their choice to discover it and fulfill
it. Even though He predestined it, He will not enforce it outside of the
person’s will. This is why God taught us to pray, ‘Thy will be done on
earth as it is in heaven’ before He does what He wills to do (Matt. 6: 10).
When we understand the immensity of the power God has placed in
man, we will know why the course and times of a man’s life is never
ordered by solely God’s predestination but his subject to human
choices. God invested so much power in man that though He is
sovereign and has the power of predestination; He still subjects Himself
to work only through the cooperation and choices of man. The
following are some powers that God invested in man:

                                                              33
                    THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

1. The Power of Imagination: At creation, God designed man to have
the power of imagination. Thus, man achieves whatever is the object of
his imagination. Thus, if a person’s imagination is not going in the
direction of God’s will and predestination for him, God can’t but allow
the person to go the way of his imagination while God seeks to route
His plans through the infinite algorithms of other possibilities to make
sure His end is still achieved.

2. The Power of Intuition: This is the cognitive ability of man to know
beyond what he sees, hears, or receives from his physical senses in the
natural. Intuition is an inner knowing and perception that makes a man
to pick certain knowledge without natural agencies of communication.
Man through intuition is supposed to know that God as God and know
His purposes and course for his live. The fundamental things to be
known about God and life is placed in man by intuition so that no one
would be with excuse (Rom1: 19 -20). Adam knew everything intuitively
before the fall but human intuition became dull by the Fall, and it is
now only sharpened by correct spiritual partnerships.

3. The Power of Passion: Passion is intense emotion expressed through
words, actions or attitude. God deposited emotional force into man to
help him in actualization of his purpose. When a person’s emotion and
passion is aligned in the direction of God’s will, God is able to ride on it
to fulfill His purpose. If one’s emotion and passion are released against
God’s will, God cannot violate it because man was designed to pursue
and achieve whatever he is passionate about.

4. The Power of Reason: This is one of the most powerful forces God
put in man. The power to think logically, make conclusions and draw a
course of action. God wants us to man to use his/her own mind and will
never violate that power.

                                                              34
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

5. The Power of the Conscience: God puts the power of inner regulation
in man so that he can always know right and wrong in life. The
conscience of man is the gentle voice that God puts in his spirit to
instruct, warn, correct and chastise so that man can be without any
excuse with regards to all the power inherent in him. A person’s
conscience can become defiled, depraved, seared, hardened, evil or
dead. When these happen, the person begins to use all the powers
invested by God in them against God. Human intuition and conscience
makes God to be justified in dealing with humans so that no one can
accuse God of unfairness in meting out consequences to people.

6. The Power of the Will: This, perhaps, is the height of the power God
has given man. The will is the power of choice, volition and self-
determination. Man wields this power so consciously that one of his
most common daily words is ‘I will …” The power of the Will, given to
man is one of the greatest expressions of God’s love, selflessness, and
self-security. The power of the Will has also placed the highest
responsibility on man. There is nothing God wants so much that He will
use His power to violate the will of the people involved. God respects
human will and will never cross the line of going against it in that
individual’s life. Thus, when the plan, purposes and preordination of
God hits against the wall of the will of the person in question, God
explores another route and means to achieve His end. God has a
predestined end in every matter which will come to pass no matter the
means and time it will take. It is good to know that it is not only the
course but also the timelines of events that are adaptable to change.
Both the course and timelines of events in this world are not cast-in-
stone by God’s predestination but by the promptness of alignment of
human will involved.

