any direction he desires and self-determine his outcome in life. Eph. 1:4
- 5 says, just as God chose us in Him before the foundation of the world,
that we should be holy and without blame before Him in love, having
predestined us to adoption as sons by Jesus Christ to Himself, according
to the good pleasure of His will. God predestines a fixed end for the
bigger picture that He is working out in every context but the fulfillment
in individual lives is neither automatic nor fixed but dependent on
individual choices. For example, God predestined salvation for all men
but people die daily without being saved - their choice. However, the
predestined end will still be achieved. So, God speaks, I have sworn by
