The Theory of Substitution in Destiny

God predestines end results but the means is subject to change based on
the choices of the persons involved. Thus, the predetermined purpose of
God will be achieved even if the human agents have to be substituted.
We should understand that, just like in a ball game, God has infinite
capable substitutes to play every role in his scheme.

Many scriptures point to the fact that Jesus was predestined to die on
the cross. Acts 2: 23 says, Jesus, being delivered by the predetermined
purpose and foreknowledge of God, you have taken by lawless hands, have
crucified, and put to death (NLT). It was predestined that Jesus Christ
would die on the cross and that one of His twelve disciples would be the
one to betray him to his death. Thus, Jesus in John 17: 12 says, during
my time here, I protected them by the power of the name you gave me. I
guarded them so that not one was lost, except the one headed for
destruction, as the Scriptures foretold.

                                                              39
                    THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

Scriptures preordained and foretold that one disciple would betray
