is found in the story of Esau and Jacob. In Gen. 25:23, predestination
was recorded when God said to Rebekah, "The sons in your womb will
become two nations. From the very beginning, the two nations will be
rivals. One nation will be stronger than the other; and your older son will
serve your younger son. People have asked if God was rather unfair in
predestining one child to be greater than the other, when neither have
even lived or done anything. Rom. 9:10-15 addressed the sentiment; ‘…
Our ancestor Isaac, when he married Rebekah, she gave birth to twins.
But before they were born, before they had done anything good or bad,

                                                              41
