Understanding Destiny

Destiny is God's plan concerning you which exists even before your
existence. To fulfill destiny, you need to need to discover God’s mind
about every area of your life and then align your will and choices
towards it. Prayer is one of the highest wisdom for living – above all
other applications; it is the tool for discovering God’s mind, will and
preordination for your every area of your destiny.

                                                              46
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

You cannot just choose any course, path or thing in life as you wish.
You need to discover God’s mind concerning the things of your life and
partner your choices along with the discovered course. Also, it is
important to know that if a particular course is not yours to fulfill, no
amount of exertion and choice can make you fulfill it. Wasted efforts in
destiny, at times, are due to pursuing a course that is out of
preordination for one. It does not mean that one may not even succeed
in that course in material terms but even at that, it is still an eternal
waste of effort. As commonly said, success in the wrong assignment is
still failure. So, the first step in destiny is to prayerfully discover God’s
preordination for one. This is what the entire premise of the Volume
One of this book is about.
Having discovered God’s planned course for your life, it is crucial to
note that it is not automatic, you have to consistently align your choices
in the direction of God’s preordination for your life to fulfill destiny.
For predestination to be fulfilled, a person needs to play his own part.
Thus, man is the truly determinant of his destiny by his choices.
Predestination and choices are like two wheels of a bicycle -
predestination is the front wheel and choices are the rear wheel. Remove
one and realize how helpless the other is.
Predestination sets the course of life and choices order the course of life.
It is important to pay great attention to the course of our lives and
make sure it is trending in the positive direction. This is done by the
choices we make at every point in our lives. How far one would go in
the direction of preordination is also dependent on our choices. It is one
thing for God to predestine you for an assignment; it is another thing to
be successful in that assignment. Put differently, even along the path of
your predestination, your choices determine how far you would go. For
instance, if God says you will be rich, it is your choice that determines
whether you will be a millionaire, billionaire or trillionaire.

                                                              47
                    THE COURSE OF LIFE PREDESTINATION AND CHIOCES

 So, if you have discovered your destiny, you also have to choose how
far you want to go in fulfilling it.
For instance, if a person who is predestined to go into academics but
due to nonchalance and wrong choices finishes school with a pass, that
person may be limited more than someone who graduated with a first
class. Also, if two people are called into the academia and one chooses
to make the sacrifices to bag a doctoral degree, he will go further that
the person who stopped at a first degree. God ordains but people
