and greatness in such discovery are parameters of choice.
When you discover and understand your destiny, choices and decisions
of life become easier. Whether marriage choices or profession choices,
all is premised on the purpose discovered.

                                                              48
                                 CHAPTER 5

             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

Along the route of a journey, there are sign posts on the way. Some of
these show direction while some reinforce assurance that one is on
course. Therefore, if one sets out for Lagos, drives for 4 hours along a
Nigerian road and sees a sign reading, ‘Lagos 1000 Km Ahead’, he
knows that he is headed in the right direction. It is when you set out for
Lagos and after driving for 6 hours, you see a sign reading, ‘Abuja 1000
Km Ahead, Kaduna 1500 Km Ahead’ that you know there is a
problem. Along the course of life, there are landmarks and milestones
that show progress and success in life.

It is important to know that progress in the realm of life is measured by
growth and not the passage of time. The signposts along the course of
life are events. Landmark events at every point indicate progress along
the course of life. The fact that one has marked spent many years is not
necessarily a measure of progress. The measure of progress along the
time-line of life is what progressive events have happened in those
years. This is the error of those who pride themselves in the
chronological passage of time and claim seniority based on age and not
results.There are people who claim ‘spiritual seniority’ because they
have been born again for 35 years. They are not aware that such
concepts do not exist in the realm of the spirit. In the realm of life, the
measure of progress along the timeline is events, milestones and
achievements.

                                                              49
                                             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

So before you boast that you got born again in 1965 before the pastor
was born, what impact have you made for the kingdom? How far have
you gone in fulfilling your Kingdom purpose? At what spiritual heights
are you operating now based on the results you are commanding in the
realm of life for the Kingdom? These parameters are what measure
progress in the spirit and not the passage of chronological time. Age, in
the realm of the spirit and in life, is measured by progressive growth,
impact and attainment, not by the passage of time.

This understanding makes one to be result-oriented in life and in
spiritual pursuits. There are milestone achievements along the course
of your life that shows that you are growing and making progress in
life. Staying at one point without progressive achievement shows you
are not moving in life. A 25 year old that is born-again, has discovered
purpose and is actively pursuing it, probably happily married and
successfully building a godly family, financially doing well and
probably a multi-millionaire, and is making impact for God’s kingdom
is ‘older’ than the 40-year-old that is moving around life with nothing
working – no purpose, no job, no working marriage, zero finance,
worse off, a liability to everyone around. Real age is not measured in
life by measured by the passage of time but progress along the time-
lines of life.
Similarly, age in the spirit is not measured by how long one has been in
the faith but by spiritual accomplishment in the direction of God’s
purpose and preordination for your life. Salvation is the gate to the
Kingdom. There are people that got born-again 35 years ago and have
not left the gate but sat at the gate-post. While there are people who
got born again two years ago and have gone far in exploring the
lifestyle of the Kingdom.

                                                              50
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

Don’t fall into the self-deception of rating how long you have been
born-again, when you joined church or how long you have been a
minister. What accomplishments, impact and milestones are you
achieving and landmark are you crossing in life. What additional
accomplishment did you have this year. Stagnation is years passing
without additional life accomplishment.

Concepts of Time-Line in Life - Chronos and Kairos

There are many Greek words translated as ‘time’ in the English Bible.
However, three of such words carry strong imports to the context of
the discussion on understanding at the timelines of life. The words
Chronos, Kairos and Aeon, among others, are translated as time in the
Bible and carry different diminution and significances. Adequate
understanding of these words helps in conveying the significance of
timing and timelines in life.

The Greek Word ‘Chronos’ (Strong NT 5550) talks about the passage
of time and a progression of space of time. This is the etymological
root of the word chronological. Chronos, as a concept, describes the
continuous passage of time in life. What you do with the chronological
passage of every second, minute, hour, day and year of your life
determines where your life is headed. In fact, Chronos is the most
important time concept in determining the outcome of your life
because your life essentially is a summation of what you do with the
chronos of life
However, another powerful concept of time is revealed by the Greek
word Kairos (Strong NT:165) which describes a particular point in time
or period. The word Kairos is usually translated in the context of an
appointed time, particular time or set time.

                                                              51
                                             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

It is important to maximize the chronological passage of time in your
life but we must be wise to know that not all times carry equal
significance in life. There are Kairos moments when something that
can change your life presents itself before you. The word Kairos is also
translated ‘opportunity’ is several places in the Bible. Missing Kairos is
one of the reasons for failure in life and maximizing Kairos is one of
the hallmarks of a great man in life. Do not waste your chronos, spend
it doing things that move you forward in destiny. Both Chronos and
Kairos need to be maximized for life to attain its fullest potential. The
daily passage of time in your life is to be used judiciously and definite
moments need to be capitalized upon.
When people sleep and play all day, squander time on things that are
irrelevant to destiny, invest time in unproductive relationships and
activities, they are squandering the Chronos of their lives. It is actually
with Chronos that you prepare for Kairos. Chronos is the real
powerhouse of life because if Chronos is not maximized, Kairos comes
and it meets no prepared foundation in place to deliver its expected
results. How you spend your time daily is the real differential of your
destiny. In Heb. 4:7, Bible says, again He designates a certain day,
saying in David, "Today," after such a long time (Chronos), as it has
been said: "Today, if you will hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.”
For a long chronos, there was no urgent visitation but wise people
maximize their chronos till a kairos comes with an opportunity.
According to John 5:2-4, Now there is in Jerusalem by the Sheep Gate a
pool, which is called in Hebrew, Bethesda, having five porches. 3 In these
lay a great multitude of sick people, blind, lame, paralyzed, waiting for the
moving of the water. For an angel went down at a certain time (Kairos)
into the pool and stirred up the water; then whoever stepped in first, after
the stirring of the water, was made well of whatever disease he had.

                                                              52
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

Kairos times are life changing moments, how you respond to
opportune time is a direct prediction of how far your life will go. There
are conversations, people, openings, meetings or requests that present
you with Kairos moments. All times are not the same, recognizing and
discerning time is a hallmark of wisdom. Eph. 5:15-18 captures the
thought well, see then that you walk circumspectly, not as fools but as
wise, redeeming the time (Kairos), because the days are evil. Therefore do
not be unwise, but understand what the will of the Lord is. Some
translations substitute the phrase ‘redeeming the time’ with ‘making the
most of opportunity’. The word Kairos means opportune time, set
time, or a particular time. There will always come a particular time
when your life will change if you discern correctly the time and
maximize the moment by doing what you need to do promptly. Some
people are wasting their daily Chronos, slacking and dishonoring
Kairos moments and wondering why nothing is happening in their life
your lifetime is determined by your use of your time in life.

The last word of interest is the word, Aeion (Greek NT 165) and it
means an age, dispensation or period. It is used to denote lifespans,
decades, centuries, millennia, or eternity. The word is translated as
‘forever and ever’ in some contexts. Eph. 3:21 says Unto him be glory in
the church by Christ Jesus throughout all ages (Genea), world without
end (Aeion to Aeion). Amen. Col. 1:26 says, even the mystery which
hath been hid from ages (Aeion) and from generations (Genea), but
now is made manifest to his saints.
If you view the Aeion as your lifetime, then Chronos is the timeline
along your lifetime and Kairos presents opportunities for milestones
and events that make your life. It is important to know that you have a
role to play in determining the timings of your life.

                                                              53
                                             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

Do you know that even the time of attainment of things in life is not
solely by God’s predestination? It is also by choice. Many times, the
timelines of events are delayed not because God does not want them to
happen yet but because the human factors have not properly aligned.
People excuse things not happening for them by saying, ‘God’s time is
the best’ when God is actually waiting for them to align and make the
time happen. If we do not maximise the times of life - the Chronos and
Kairos, the Aeion (the lifetime) suffers for it. Things do not happen and
we think that it is because it is not yet time by God’s calendar whereas
it is because we have not made it happen by our engagement of time
here on earth.

Waiting Times and Appointed Times

There are Kairos moments in destiny. Appointed times are not every
time – there are specific times when destiny comes knocking, and
opening the door and apprehending it could mean the difference
between failure and success forever. This is why it is important to know
how to persevere and wait till your appointed time comes. Job 14:14
says, ‘... all the days of my appointed time will I wait, till my change
come’.
Waiting time is an integral part of the times of life, unfortunately the
concept of waiting time has been grossly misunderstood by many and it
has led to gross limitations in destiny. Milestones and events of life are
delivered at appointed times but in-between appointed moments are
the waiting times. According to Hab. 2:3, for the vision is yet for an
appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry,
wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry. Waiting time is
simply the Chronos in between the Kairos moments. Many people think
waiting means staying in a limbo in expectation of something from God

                                                              54
                                                TIMES AND SEASON

while doing nothing.
There are people who finish school doing nothing and when asked,
they say they are waiting for a job. The concept of waiting doing
nothing is an abuse of life. Waiting time is simply the Chronos that
leads to the Kairos you are expecting. The grossest misunderstanding is
displayed when someone says they are waiting on God and they are not
doing anything but praying, reading Bible and largely sleeping while
not working at anything productive with their lives. Therefore, for
every expectation in life, there must be something you are doing
actively in preparing for the opportune moment. Waiting actually is
whatever you are busy doing in anticipation of the Kairos moment you
are expecting. Therefore, you can be waiting to start the vision or call
upon your life while you are busy working at a job or serving in an
existing vision. You are waiting for a job while you are in school or
studying a postgraduate course. You are waiting to start your business
while you are working as an employee under someone doing a similar
thing. A person is waiting for marriage while busy putting structures of
establishment in place for his/her life. Waiting is not a passive state; it
is an active state of life. In fact, everyone in life is waiting. The
millionaire is waiting to become a billionaire so she is busy every day
working at her million dollar business while waiting and praying for
that big break - the appointed time – that launches her into the billion
level. The medical student is waiting to become a medical doctor and is
aware that it is the quality of her investment and performance in this
‘waiting period’ as a student that determines the quality of her prospect
at the appointed time after graduation. Waiting periods are busy
period, not sleeping period. Anyone who is doing nothing and claims
he/she is waiting, is actually wasting and dying.
People say they are waiting on God while God is waiting for them. It is

                                                              55
                                             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

what you are doing now that will lead to what you will do next. It is the
Chronos that leads to the Kairos – so the waiting time leads to the
appointed time. When the waiting time is spent doing nothing, the
appointed time has no in-flow to make it happen. Waiting time is
actually the preparation time before any breakthrough. Therefore,
appointed times can be triggered by the quality of maximization of the
preparing time. God is the one that appoints time. Isa. 61:1-3 is a
prophecy about Jesus Christ, the Spirit of the Lord God is upon me;
because the Lord hath anointed me to proclaim the acceptable year of the
Lord, and the day of vengeance of our God; to comfort all that mourn; to
appoint unto them that mourn in Zion,

God is the one who appoints time. Ex 9:5 says, the Lord appointed a set
time, saying, tomorrow the Lord shall do this thing in the land. God is the
God of appointed times. However, we have also seen men appoint
times. Examples are Elijah in 1 Kings 17 who declared that rain would
not fall for the next three and a half years until he changes the time and
Elisha in 2 Kings 7:1-2 who decreed that the famine would end the next
day.
The power of the prophetic is changing times and season is untold.
Therefore, you can hold to a prophetic word from God and on the
strength of that and enforce a Kairos moment on your life. Faith and
prayers are spiritual forces for birthing forth an appointed time.
Therefore, if the appointed time seems not to be coming, having
labored in prayers over the issue, I can rise up in faith and by the Spirit
of God declare that my appointed time has come. According to Psa.
102: 13, You will arise and have mercy on Zion; For the time to favor her,
Yes, the set time, has come. You can ride on the strength of faith in
God’s word, decide that your appointed time is now and insist on it
until you get.

                                                              56
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

When working out your faith for an appointed time, an integral
component of that faith walk is that you channel the waiting time to
putting everything in place like someone sure that the appointed time
has come. Thus, for instance, if you have prayed, received the Word of
God, and you believe that your appointed time for child-birth has
come, you should quit waiting passively and convert the waiting period
to the preparation period for your baby’s birth. God gives a provision
in the spirit for man to appoint his/her own time but then it must be by
faith and the faith is best evidenced in how you use the waiting period
after you have decreed yourself an appointed time.

Missing Timings in Life

One of the worst things in life and the most common cause of life
failure is missing timing in life. Some people fail in life because they did
not get what to do right. Some fail because they did not get the timing
of their lives right. Ps. 32:9 says, do not be like the horse or the mule,
which have no understanding but must be controlled by bit and bridle or
they will not come to you. The horse and the mule do not have
understanding of time so they get bloodied mouths. The bridle and bits
used on horses and oxen are very painful instruments as they are yoked
to their mouth system to control them. The problem with the horse is
that it does not understand timing so it has high propensity to be too
fast for its owner, so the rider puts a painful bit in its mouth to slow it
down and control it. The mule, on its own part, used to plough the
farm, has no understanding of timing so it is too slow for the farmer.
So, they use the yoke in its mouth to drag it. The pain of yoking any
animal’s mouth is extreme. It is only imaginable when you consider it
to be your mouth where those iron or wooden pegs are driven and
connect to a haul which is used to either drag you forward or
backward. The pain of not understanding timing in life is equally

                                                              57
                                             THE TIME-LINE OF LIFE

immense. Whether one runs ahead in destiny or slows down
unnecessarily in destiny, the pain is always failure or regrets. The only
way to enjoy destiny is to be in pace with your life. This happens when
you accurately sense the timings of your life.

It is not just important to know what God wants you to do. You must
always ask God when. It is a disaster to run ahead when God does not
yet say to move. It is equally a calamity to stay when God has already
told you to move. You must make sure your destiny is in sync with
God’s will. We get timings right in life, when we are people devoted to
prayers.

Missing timings in life can lead to irrecoverable loss. In Luke 19:41 -
44, Jesus wept over Jerusalem and said, "If you, even you, had only
known on this day what would bring you peace — but now it is hidden
from your eyes. The days will come upon you when your enemies will build
an embankment against you and encircle you and hem you in on every
side. They will dash you to the ground, you and the children within your
walls. They will not leave one stone on another, because you did not
recognize the time of God's coming to you" (NIV). The entire
catastrophe that befell them was because they did not recognize their
appointed time came and they missed timing in life. You have to be
diligent in maximizing your Chronos, you have to be really prayerful
and daily at alert. If Kairos comes and one missed it, one may never
recover or may have to wait untold number of years in pain because
one missed timing; either moving when it was time to staying or staying
when it was time to move.

God's Assignment - The Kingdom

Life is all about Times and Seasons. Living a great life is all about
maximizing each season of life.

                                                              58
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

A common mistake in life is people wishing and praying for a great life
while neglecting to greatly utilize the season of life they are in. A great
live is simply a sum total of greatness of each season of life. There is no
how that one can make something great out of life in the absence of a
profound understanding of all ramifications of time in life as portrayed
in this book. Healthy relationship with time in all its ramifications is a
principal determinant of success and fulfillment in life.
Eccl. 9:11 says I have seen something else under the sun. The race is not
to the swift or the battle to the strong, nor does food come to the wise or
wealth to the brilliant or favor to the learned; but time and chance happen
to them all. (NIV). God’s wisdom in this scripture listed all the
parameters that make for success in life: strength, brilliance, skills,
education and many other things but concluded by saying that beyond
all these, the singular determinant of success is timing and opportunity.
A strong or talented person who is not aligned with timing in destiny
will always be behind the weaker or less talented person who always
gets the timings of his/her right.

                                                              59
                                 CHAPTER 6

             RESTORATION OF TIME
               AND SEASON IN LIFE

Due Season

There is something as due season in life. Ps. 1:3 says, and he shall be
like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his
season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall
prosper.
There is a due season for everything in life. When the time you should
have had a result is passed and it is not forthcoming, it should become
an issue of concern. Delay, belated life and denial are satanic strategies
for causing failure in life. If time is going and the milestones are not
coming, then such life is running behind schedule and unless there is
divine intervention, failure or short-changing of destiny is imminent.
We should demand for the fruits of our life in due season. When it is
time to get a thing in life, then it must be demanded from life.

For instance, it is not just important to be established and helped
in life. It is important that it happens early. Ps. 46:5 says, God is
in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, and
that right early. When seasons are delayed and fruits are belated,
they cost a person’s destiny so much. The best of life is in things
happening at the right time and milestones being achieved right
early in life – at the right time.

                                                              60
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

There is a right time to build a house - it is not with your gratuity after
retirement when your children are already on their way out to get
married and start their own families. There is a right time to be rich,
married, start your vision or ministry. There is a due season for every
fruit. Wisdom is knowing the achievement, milestone that is due in your
life by now and going for it and not just leaving your life to chance and
coursing through life, expecting things to happen when they want to.
You should know that by God’s calendar for my life, I should be a
millionaire by now. I should have started my vision by now. I should be
married with children. You have to know the chronos timetable of God
for your life and insist on Kairos moments to deliver the milestones that
are due along spiritual timeline of your life as revealed by God’s
timetable/calendar of your life

Zech. 10:1 says, Ask ye of the Lord rain in the time of the latter rain; so
the Lord shall make bright clouds, and give them showers of rain, to every
one grass in the field. When you see that it is supposed to be time for
rain in your life and the rain is not coming, you had better started
praying and fasting for rain. Do not leave life to chance, when you see
that it is time for anything to happen and it is not happening, you must
take spiritual responsibility and start demanding from heaven that the
times of your life be aligned with God’s calendar for you.

Being out of Season

There is not only what God wants you to do in life, there is a calendar
of progress he has for you. Satan tries all his best to prevent people
from discovering what they should do with their lives. The moment he
has failed by one giving his/her life to Christ and discovering purpose
and destiny. One strong strategy he has left is to resist the path so much
that one’s preordained timeline is slowed down. This is because there
are two ways to fail an exam: not knowing the right answers or knowing
the right answers but not having enough time to answer them. So, if
satan sees that he has failed in derailing a person’s course of life, he will
insist on resisting their time of line. According to Rev.12:12, Satan has a
short time so he understands the disadvantage that shortness of time

                                                              61
                            RESTORATION OF TIME AND SEASON IN LIFE

Thus, he fights people on the issue of time. Begin to pray
vehemently about the times of your life and insist on certain
things that must happen at certain times. Do not take the issue of
time gently in life; so many people are failing because the enemy is
winning them on the issue of time. Clichés like ‘God’s time is the
best’, ‘it is all well that ends well’, ‘e go better - tomorrow will be
better’, etc. have made many people to be deceived by the enemy
not to know that we are in a warfare over the time of our life.
Today, insist in the name of Jesus that now is the time for your
breakthrough, marriage, business and ministry to start, or any
other thing for that matter that you know should be due in your
life right now.

Restoration of Wasted Time - The Mercy of God

Time is one commodity that once it is gone, you can never have it back.
You may have another opportunity another time but that one that was
squandered is gone. Every one has 24 hours in a day and for every time
that is wasted, a part of life is gone. This is the reason one of satan’s
strategies of warfare is to fight your times of life. If satan cannot stop
you, he will do all he can to delay you. He knows for every time you
spend in stagnation unable to proceed, he has won a part of your life.
Thus, praying for God to deliver for you on time is a vital warfare
prayer in destiny.

Even the times that has been squandered in the time past by ignorance,
disobedience and satanic siege can be recovered by the mercy of God.
When God restores the time of your life, He takes you to where you
should be right now had it been there was no disadvantage at any point
of your timeline in destiny. It is important to pray for recovery of time,
especially if things have happened in the time past that have slowed,
derailed or delayed the time and course of your life at any point.

                                                              62
                                        TIMES AND SEASONS OF LIFE

God says in Joel 2:25 - 27, and I will restore to you the years that
the locust hath eaten, the cankerworm, and the caterpillar, and the
palmer worm, my great army which I sent among you. And ye shall
eat in plenty, and be satisfied, and praise the name of the Lord your
God, that hath dealt wondrously with you: and my people shall
never be ashamed. And ye shall know that I am in the midst of
Israel, and that I am the Lord your God, and none else: and my
people shall never be ashamed. Today, every shame is wiped away
from your life and every lost time is recovered in Jesus name.

Time lost can be recovered only by the mercy of GOD. Psa. 102:
13 says, You will arise and have mercy on Zion; For the time to
favor her, Yes, the set time, has come. It is time to cry out for
mercy over the times of your life. Every time of your life that was
lost, squandered or stolen by the enemy is restored by the mercy
of God in Jesus name.

Conclusively, a great course in the School of Wisdom is the
course on time. Wisdom is knowing what to do, when to do it,
how to do it, with whom to do it, and where to do it. Failure can
ensue by missing any out of these five adverbs of wisdom, even
when you get the others right.

So never forget to keep the brevity of your lifetime in perpetual
view and go all out to maximize life. Two scriptural reference that
should guide your life in relating with your time of life are ‘Lord,
please teach us to realize the brevity of life so that we may grow in
wisdom the time of your life.’ (Ps. 90:12 NLT) and ‘know the
importance of the season you’re in and a wise son you will be. But
what a waste when an incompetent son.’ (Prov 10: 5).

